            <li>Improve messaging functionality</li>
            <li>Add analytics and monitoring</li>
            <li>Further optimise mobile performance</li>
        </ul>
    </div>


    <!-- SECTION 14: LOCAL SETUP -->
    <div class="readme-section">
        <h2>13. Running the Project Locally</h2>

        <h3>Step 1 – Install dependencies</h3>

        <div class="project-structure">
npm install
        </div>

        <h3>Step 2 – Start the application</h3>

        <div class="project-structure">
npm start
        </div>

        <h3>Step 3 – Open the application</h3>

        <div class="project-structure">
http://localhost:8000
        </div>
    </div>


    <!-- SECTION 15: ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES -->
    <div class="readme-section">
        <h2>14. Environment Variables</h2>

        <p>
            Sensitive configuration values should be stored using environment
            variables rather than being hard-coded in the source code.
        </p>

        <div class="project-structure">
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
SESSION_SECRET=your_session_secret
PORT=8000
        </div>
    </div>


    <!-- SECTION 16: DEPLOYMENT -->
    <div class="readme-section">
        <h2>15. Deployment</h2>

        <p>
            The application can be deployed as a Node.js web service using a
            cloud hosting platform such as Render.
        </p>

        <p>
            The deployment should use the production environment variables
            and the hosting platform's assigned PORT.
        </p>
    </div>


    <!-- SECTION 17: GITHUB -->
    <div class="readme-section">
        <h2>16. Source Code</h2>

